.TH prep "" "Command"
.SH NAME
prep \- produce a word list
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBprep [\-dfp] [\-i \fIfile\fB] [\-o \fIfile\fB] [\fIfile ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
prep -- produce a word list
Usage:	prep [ options ]  [ file ... ]
Options:
	-d	Print number of each word output
	-f	Fold upper case to lower case
	-i file	Ignore all words in 'file' on output
	-o file	Output only words from 'file'
	-p	Print punctuation marks on separate lines (not numbered)
Text is taken from each input 'file' or the standard input if none.
Words consist of alphabetic characters and apostrophes.
.HE
.B prep
breaks the text of each input
.I file
(or the standard input, if none is named) into words and writes them,
one per line, to the standard output.
A word is a run of alphabetic characters and apostrophes; a hyphen
followed immediately by a newline joins the word before it to the
word after, and any other hyphen ends the current word.
.PP
.B prep
recognizes the following options; they are given before any
.IR file :
.IP \fB\-d\fR
Precede each output word with its word number in the input (a count
of words seen so far), followed by a tab.
.IP \fB\-f\fR
Fold upper-case letters to lower case as each character is read.
.IP "\fB\-i \fIfile\fR"
Read a list of words, one per line, from
.IR file ,
and do not output any input word that matches one of them.
.B \-i
and
.B \-o
may not both be given.
.IP "\fB\-o \fIfile\fR"
Read a list of words, one per line, from
.IR file ,
and output only input words that match one of them.
.B \-i
and
.B \-o
may not both be given.
.IP \fB\-p\fR
Also write each punctuation character (any non-alphabetic, printable
character outside a word) to the standard output, alone on its own
line; these lines are not counted for
.BR \-d .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR deroff ,
.BR sort ,
.BR spell ,
.BR typo ,
.B wc
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B prep
complains and exits if
.B \-i
and
.B \-o
are both given, if the file named by
.B \-i
or
.B \-o
cannot be opened, or if any input
.I file
cannot be opened.
.SH NOTES
What counts as a
.I word
differs among
.BR deroff ,
.BR prep ,
and
.BR wc .
